                {
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "content": "About this project",
                      "fill": "#F2F2F2",
                      "fontFamily": "Space Grotesk",
                      "fontSize": 22,
                      "fontWeight": "600",
                      "id": "n2RIyI",
                      "name": "About Title",
                      "type": "text"
                    },
                    {
                      "content": "Smart Garden Monitor is a compact IoT device that continuously measures soil moisture, light and temperature for balcony and indoor gardens. When the soil dries below a set threshold, it triggers an automated drip pump and notifies the owner in the companion app.",
                      "fill": "#C8C8C8",
                      "fontFamily": "Space Grotesk",
                      "fontSize": 15,
                      "fontWeight": "normal",
                      "id": "y6CVaA",
                      "lineHeight": 1.55,
                      "name": "P1",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "type": "text",
                      "width": "fill_container"
                    },
                    {
                      "content": "The team built the firmware on an ESP32, designed a 3D-printed weatherproof enclosure, and shipped a small Next.js dashboard for historical charts. It was completed as part of the Web Development course in winter term 2024.",
